    "evidence_text": "New Venice School\n\nJoaqu\u00edn Rodrigo\n\nDas Marienleben\n\nDas Marienleben (\"The Life of Mary\") is a song cycle by German composer Paul Hindemith.\n\nWDR Rundfunkchor K\u00f6ln\n\n It was founded in 1947.\n\nJohann Strauss III\n\nAl gran sole carico d'amore\n\n Nono himself and Yuri Lyubimov wrote the libretto.\n\n In addition to vocal soloists, chorus and orchestra, the work incorporates taped sounds.\n\nSuvini Zerboni\n\n The ESZ catalalogue of modern Italian composers active since the 1970s is extensive.\n\n ESZ also publishes the bulletin \u201cESZ News\u201d with information on the activities and performances of its composers.\n\nHenryk G\u00f3recki\n\n According to critic Alex Ross, no recent classical composer has had as much commercial success as G\u00f3recki.\n\nDorothy Dorow\n\n Dorow debuted in London in 1958.\n\n She is also noted for her performances of the vocal works of Igor Stravinsky.\n\n Dorow performed internationally including at the Krak\u00f3w Philharmonic.\n\nPaul Hindemith",
